# Retail, "Mainline" in Blizzard's own flavour vocabulary (COMPAT-2). Same file list as Kitbag.toc — the flavour difference is confined to
# KitbagCompat.lua, which resolves the 11.0 C_Item / C_Spell moves and the container namespace.
#
# THE ## Interface NUMBER ABOVE IS UNVERIFIED. It was not checked against a live Retail client,
# because none was installed when this was written. A stale one shows the addon as out of date and,
# on some flavours, refuses to load it — so check it before this flavour is published.
#
# Two Retail differences are handled by absence rather than by a branch, and are worth knowing:
# there is no ranged/relic slot (inventory slot 18 simply reads empty, and CharacterRangedSlot does
# not exist, which KitbagFlyout already tolerates), and the reagent bank is detected from
# REAGENTBANK_CONTAINER rather than assumed.
KitbagCompat.lua
KitbagCore.lua
KitbagRules.lua
